today we're talking about two  budget-friendly iPads the brand-new 2019  iPad Mini and the 2019 iPad iPad what's  going on guys my name is David Tommy and  welcome back to the channel today we're  talking about two iPads and two iPads in  particular we're talking about the brand  new 2019 iPad Mini which comes in a 7.9  a Retina display and costs about 599  Australian dollars which for all your US  viewers is about 400 u.s. we're also  talking about the brand new 10.2 inch  iPad iPad it's the original iPad the one  that only has the iPad name it starts  from about 529 Australian dollars but  this one here being a cellular version  goes all the way up to seven hundred and  twenty-nine dollars for about 500 US  this one isn't so budget-friendly the  Wi-Fi only version compared to the iPad  Mini is pretty much price for price if  you're looking for a budget-friendly  iPad chances are you're not really too  interested about the specs yes they're  important but they don't mean too much  it's really about how you're going to  use your iPad and what you're planning  on using the iPad for if you are  interested in the specs spoiler alert  the iPad Mini is a much better purchase  overall it has a better user rated  battery life it has a much better screen  resolution and it also has a much better  forward facing camera a quick little  side-by-side test here with the two  iPads on each side the iPad Mini and the  iPad iPad the camera itself is pretty  decent you're not really going to be  using the camera from the iPad as your  main camera more so but what you will  notice is when you zoom in with the  iPads  the actual camera quality is quite bad  and the noise and grain is pretty heavy  for both iPads and it's no surprise at  all that the iPad Mini is forward-facing  selfie camera produces a much better  image with a seven megapixel camera  versus a 1.2 megapixel camera you are  going to get a much  a FaceTime call or just a single selfie  photo if you're looking to utilize these  features from the iPad so like I've  already said chances are you're probably  not looking at these iPads for their  specs you're looking at them to be  purpose-built towards your lifestyle so  you could be professional out there  looking for a workhorse or you could be  an average consumer out there looking  for just a media consumption base so  let's take a look at the professional  category first if you're a professional  that has to walk around all day  carry their iPad all day take a ton of  notes with the Apple pencil and really  just have to lug this thing around all  day my personal recommendation would be  the iPad Mini for the sole purpose that  it's so small so light so compact and it  doesn't feel like a burden to carry  around it's just over 200 grams and you  don't really notice it when you pick it  up when you carry it around so from a  professional point of view if you're  somebody that's just out there writing  notes taking notes and needs this thing  to be pretty much their daily driver the  iPad Mini is the best choice out of the  two but on the other hand if you're  somebody that sits in more formal  meetings day-to-day that needs a bit  more screen real estate to look at  images to blow-up images to do things a  little bit more on the creative side of  things where you need more screen real  estate well then the actual iPad iPad  which doesn't have a second name to it  is probably the better choice for you  guys with the extra large screen real  estate it is a little bit more of a  burden to carry around and you  definitely do feel the weight when  you're comparing the two it is pretty  well balanced so you don't notice it too  much but it is a burden to carry around  all day so if you're somebody that is  going into meetings and you do need some  sort of tech with you but if you open up  a full-fledged laptop everybody's going  to look at you a bit funny then the iPad  iPad is probably the best one for you  out of these two now let's say you're  not a professional you're not looking to  buy an iPad for business-related  purposes or for your work life you're  looking to buy an iPad for your own  personal joy you're looking for the iPad  to be  consumption-based to consume all the  YouTube videos out there play a few  games and no just to have a good time  with your iPad well in my personal  opinion I believe everybody's going to  steer you to the bigger larger 10.2 inch  display but I have a little bit of a  hesitation to steering you toward this  one because I don't find it as useful in  a day-to-day life purpose as an iPad  Mini everybody's phones is quite large  but they're not that large to consume a  whole bunch of content on whilst the  iPad Mini in my personal opinion is  probably just the right size for  consuming heaps of content and if we're  being completely honest with ourselves  we all probably watch content from about  20 centimeters or a so the extra screen  real estate as a memory probably won't  be too much of a difference as an added  bonus the iPad Mini also has a higher  pixel per inch ratio at 326 pixels per  inch versus the iPads 246 I believe is  off the top of my head so you're going  to get a much clearer much sharper  display from the iPad Mini with the  added benefit of the true tone display  so if you're looking for a good media  consumption device then the iPad Mini is  definitely my recommendation out of  these two even though most people will  probably steer you to the 10.2 inch  display for the sole purposes of having  a bigger display and that's all for me  guys remember don't go out and buy an  iPad for the sole purposes of specs if  one is better than the other or you're  gonna go out and pay a grand and a half  for the top-of-the-range Pro but all  you're really looking at using it for is  maybe some cooking recipes or watching a  youtube video here and there it's going  to end up in your drawer or on eBay like  the rest of the iPads you've probably  owned in the past so take a step back  think about what you're actually gonna  use this iPad for and then make your  decision based on your personal needs  not anybody else's and not the specs  themselves thanks so much for watching  guys if you haven't already make sure  you smash that subscribe button  20-19 style almost 20/20 style and as  always I'll see you next Monday

